/-!
# `row_residue` for q = 5 through `ZMod 11`

`vSeedPrime 5 = 11`.  Data (all checked exactly in Python, see `checks/`):
* `q5rzD r` is the lcm of the denominators of row `r` of
  `q5SourceMatrixAtZeroExplicit`; `q5rzN0 = diag(q5rzD) * M_0` and
  `q5rzAN = diag(q5rzD) * A` are integer matrices, so
  `diag(q5rzD) * M_t = q5rzN0 - t * q5rzAN`;
* for `t = 0..4`, `q5rzE * q5rzNbar_t = q5rzL_t * q5rzU_t` in `ZMod 11`, with
  `q5rzE` upper and `q5rzL_t` lower unitriangular, and `q5rzNbar_t` the residue of
  `q5rzN0 - t * q5rzAN`;
* `q5rzW` inverts the Vandermonde matrix `(tʲ)` modulo 11.

No rational determinant at `T ≠ 0`, no rational interpolation, and no 9 by 9
Leibniz expansion occurs.  Every `decide` acts on entries below 11, on one
`ℤ → ZMod 11` cast, on one 9-term dot product, or on the product of nine
small naturals.  Determinants are reached only through `Matrix.det_mul`,
`Matrix.det_of_isUpperTriangular`/`isLowerTriangular` and `RingHom.map_det`.
Exact coefficient residues: [5, 2, 5, 8, 7] = `vSeedResidueRow 5`.
-/

namespace Li2Lean.B3

noncomputable section

open Li2Lean
open Matrix

set_option maxRecDepth 1000000
set_option maxHeartbeats 20000000

instance q5rzFact : Fact (Nat.Prime (vSeedPrime 5)) := ⟨by norm_num [vSeedPrime]⟩

